            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Osteoporosis could contribute to increase other chronic diseases such as cardiovascular events, resulting in higher mortality in these patients. Antiresorptive agents such as bisphosphonates has been reported to reduce not only the number of fragile fracture but also all causes mortality. These agents are also expected to improve quality of life and activity of daily life with longer life expectancy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
